# MCP Tool Server

Local analysis over stdio. Not a hosted billable proxy unless explicitly building that path.

## Stdio / JSON-RPC

- Newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout. Stdout is for protocol only (no logs).
- Support `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`. Require initialize before tools.
- Negotiate protocol from supported set; default toward `2025-11-25`.
- Cap message size; on `tools/call` return `content` text (usually JSON report) + `isError`.

## Tools

- `inputSchema`: object schemas with `additionalProperties: false` when practical.
- Descriptions state limits (heuristic, not full validator; no live probes unless opt-in).
- Core logic in a separate module (`guardian.js` / `doctor.js` / `core.js`) testable without MCP.

## Packaging

- `"type": "module"`. Prefer `node --test`. Keep useful path runnable from source with absolute path in client config.
- Do not document `npx -y <pkg>` as working before publish + name ownership.
- README: tools table, privacy, limitations, commercial boundary (free local / hosted Pro later).
